# 5. High-Level Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    UI[Add Device UI] --> Coordinator[Discovery Coordinator]
    Coordinator --> Cache[Known Device Store]
    Coordinator --> Network[Network Discovery Engine]
    Coordinator --> HomeKit[HomeKit Source]
    Coordinator --> Plugins[Plugin Discovery Providers]
    Network --> Bonjour[Bonjour / mDNS]
    Network --> SSDP[SSDP when required]
    Network --> Probe[Targeted Verification Probes]
    Plugins --> Philips[Philips TV Plugin]
    Plugins --> AppleTV[Apple TV Plugin]
    Plugins --> Hue[Hue Bridge Plugin]
    Plugins --> Future[Future Plugins]
    Coordinator --> Merger[Candidate Merger]
    Merger --> Verifier[Plugin Verification]
    Verifier --> Registry[Unified Device Registry]
    Registry --> UI
    Coordinator --> Diagnostics[Discovery Diagnostics]
```

The UI must never manage network browsers, sockets, service records or vendor-specific verification directly.

The Discovery Coordinator owns the lifecycle of a discovery session and publishes normalized state to the UI.

