# 8. Discovery Session Model

A discovery session represents one bounded attempt to find devices.

```swift
struct DiscoverySession: Sendable, Identifiable {
    let id: UUID
    let startedAt: Date
    let trigger: DiscoveryTrigger
    let requestedPluginIDs: Set<PluginIdentifier>?
    let timeout: Duration
}

enum DiscoveryTrigger: Sendable, Equatable {
    case appLaunch
    case addDeviceScreen
    case userRefresh
    case networkChanged
    case reconnectKnownDevice
    case manualEntry
    case diagnostics
}
```

Only one foreground full-scan session should normally run at a time.

Targeted reconnect sessions may run independently for known devices when safely coordinated.

---

# 9. Discovery Lifecycle

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Idle
    Idle --> Preparing: start session
    Preparing --> PermissionRequired: local access unresolved
    PermissionRequired --> Discovering: permission allowed
    PermissionRequired --> Restricted: permission denied
    Preparing --> Discovering: permission already allowed
    Discovering --> Verifying: candidates found
    Discovering --> Completed: timeout with no candidates
    Verifying --> Presenting: verified results available
    Presenting --> Verifying: more candidates arrive
    Presenting --> Completed: session ends
    Discovering --> Cancelled: user leaves
    Verifying --> Cancelled: user leaves
    Discovering --> Failed: fatal system error
    Verifying --> Failed: fatal system error
    Completed --> [*]
    Cancelled --> [*]
    Failed --> [*]
    Restricted --> [*]
```

Recommended internal state:

```swift
enum DiscoverySessionState: Sendable, Equatable {
    case idle
    case preparing
    case permissionRequired
    case discovering(progress: DiscoveryProgress)
    case verifying(candidateCount: Int)
    case presenting(resultCount: Int, isStillSearching: Bool)
    case completed(resultCount: Int)
    case restricted(DiscoveryRestriction)
    case cancelled
    case failed(DiscoveryError)
}
```

