# 13. Duplicate Detection and Merging

Duplicate handling is a central platform responsibility.

The same physical device may appear through:

- Cached records
- Bonjour
- SSDP
- HomeKit
- Hue Bridge resources
- Manual entry
- Multiple network interfaces

## 13.1 Identity Priority

Preferred identity order:

1. Exact plugin-defined stable identifier
2. Vendor bridge or accessory identifier
3. Trusted serial number
4. Previously stored pairing relationship
5. Strong multi-field match
6. User confirmation

IP address alone must never be treated as sufficient proof of identity.

## 13.2 Merge Confidence

```swift
enum MergeConfidence: Sendable, Comparable {
    case none
    case weak
    case probable
    case strong
    case exact
}
```

Automatic merge is allowed only for strong or exact matches.

Probable matches may be merged internally only when the user-facing result remains reversible and diagnostics preserve the source routes.

Weak matches must remain separate unless the user confirms they represent the same device.

## 13.3 Multiple Control Routes

Aura may retain multiple internal routes to the same logical device.

Example:

```text
Logical Hue Light
├── Direct Hue Bridge route
└── HomeKit route
```

The Unified Device Registry should select a preferred route according to reliability, latency, capability completeness and user configuration.

The user should normally see one device.

