# 35. Acceptance Criteria

The Device Discovery System is ready for initial release when:

- Known paired devices appear immediately from local storage
- Supported local devices can be discovered without manual configuration where the integration permits it
- Discovery results appear progressively
- The same device is not shown repeatedly when found by multiple sources
- Stable identifiers are used instead of IP addresses for long-term identity
- Local-network permission denial is handled clearly
- No broad unrestricted port scan is performed
- Vendor-specific candidates are verified by the responsible plugin
- One provider failure does not stop other discovery sources
- Discovery can be cancelled without leaked tasks or browsers
- Network changes trigger safe targeted recovery
- Manual entry works for supported integrations
- Cached devices remain available as offline records when the network is unavailable
- Add Device UI remains responsive throughout discovery
- Diagnostics expose useful session information without secrets
- Core discovery behavior is covered by automated tests
- Real hardware discovery passes for the initial supported device set

